# Cloudflare-native header rules (Workers Static Assets + Pages both read
# this file). Scoped to the unhashed public/ media files only — anything
# Vite fingerprints (assets/*-HASH.js/css) already gets a content hash in
# its filename, so it's safe to cache far longer; that's handled by
# Cloudflare's own defaults for those, not this file.
#
# 1 day, not "immutable"/1 year: these filenames don't change when the
# content does (no content hash), so a returning visitor should pick up an
# updated Hero3.mp4/logo.png etc. within a day of a redeploy rather than
# being stuck on a stale cached copy for months.
/*.mp4
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
